// Scenarios are the ways to start a game; the player picks one on New game.
// `start` is the first location. `setup` runs first and quietly (items, feats,
// values), then `intro` is shown as the opening scene.

== scenario woodland_start
name: The cabin
start: cabin
description: You wake in a small cabin at the edge of the Quiet Woods.
setup:
    ~ give wild_berries quietly
intro:
    You wake to birdsong and the smell of cold ashes. Your cabin is quiet, and the woods outside are waiting.
    ---
    [weather] Somewhere out there, the hermit who lives in the clearing will want to meet you.

== scenario forager_start
name: The forager
start: clearing
description: You have spent the summer foraging in the woods. You know the berry patches, and you carry your own knife.
setup:
    ~ give carving_knife quietly
    ~ give herbal_tea quietly
    ~ feat + forager quietly
    ~ discover cabin quietly
intro:
    You stretch beside the mossy stones of the clearing, a basket of berries at your feet. Another day of foraging.
